{
  "openrpc": "1.3.2",
  "info": {
    "title": "ae/media-session",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Video calls through LiveKit. Server (server/video.ts, WebCrypto only, tagged server): grants and room listing. Browser (web/video.ts, class Video over livekit-client 2.23.0, tagged web). Apple (@MainActor final class VideoSession over LiveKit 2.19.0, tagged swift) and Android (class ae.video.VideoSession over livekit-android 2.29.0, tagged kotlin). Browser: the constructor listens for modeEvent; publish the initial display mode before connecting; a false canCapture on that event disconnects and forgets the grant; generation checks reject stale completions. Apple: call on the main actor; the caller disconnects on display entry. Android: call from the main thread; the caller calls forget on display entry or room leave. Server: the authenticated recipe supplies participant identity and the room prefix, uses publish false for spectators and issues no grant for a display; room routes enforce authentication and privacy. Native dependency versions and locks are in tests/native/dependencies.json; the verification helpers aepm's runner calls are in interfaces/media-session-verification.json.",
    "license": {
      "name": "Apache-2.0",
      "url": "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
    }
  },
  "methods": [
